{"id":"belt_squat","name":"Belt squat","cue":"Stand tall; sit down between your knees, the load hangs from your hips.","research":"Belt squat on a plate-loaded lever machine (science audit table B: the belt or V squat as a hack squat alternative; deep squats train the quads and the glutes alike, Kubo 2019; the bar-free load spares the spine, the cue is to stay tall). Standing on two raised platforms (0.2 H, soles flat, 0.12 H either side of the midline, toes out 15 deg, solved by foot IK), a weighted belt around the hips (the ring is fitted to the skin at the belt line of the pelvis), a chain from the belt ring down between the knees to a lever arm that pivots on the front frame (0.5 H ahead of the chain point, plates on horns at its rear end), hands on two vertical handles on the front frame (solved by IK, elbows 50 to 80 deg). The arm angle per key keeps the chain a constant 0.30 H long (arm -16 deg at the bottom to +14 at the top, the plate bottoms swinging between 0.06 H above the floor and 0.55 H up behind the lifter). Bottom: knee 120, hip 107, ankle 28, trunk 22 deg forward of vertical with the spine neutral; top: standing with soft knees (8), trunk 3. The hip height is solved from the knee angle at both ends and runs linearly between, the hips travel back 0.115 H. Muscles: the quads (three heads) and the glutes.","targets":{"tol":10,"tolBy":{"elbow_flexion":25,"shoulder_elevation":20,"ankle_dorsiflexion":8},"note":"Design values: a deep belt squat with the trunk tall; elbow and shoulder angles are the IK solution for the fixed handles.","A":{"trunk_flexion":22,"hip_flexion":107,"knee_flexion":120,"ankle_dorsiflexion":28},"B":{"trunk_flexion":3,"hip_flexion":6,"knee_flexion":8,"ankle_dorsiflexion":2}},"muscles":{"primary":["vast_lat","rect_fem","vast_med","glute_max"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":90,"el":10,"dAz":-28,"dEl":0,"fill":0.62,"note":"Research view az 90 (profile: depth, the hips travelling back and the lever swinging behind). Turned